// test-error
// Issue #1133: the residual include-guard collision is diagnosed, not silent.
//
// Keying the guard on the relative path (ADR-063) separates same-basename files
// in different directories, but uppercasing is still a lossy map: `-` and `_`
// both sanitize to `_`, so mod-a.cnx and mod_a.cnx share CNX_MOD_A_H. Filenames
// differing only by case collapse the same way.
//
// ADR-063 handles that residue with E0203 rather than a hash or an escape
// encoding, on the grounds that two files in one build differing only by `-`
// versus `_` are confusing to a human reader before they are confusing to the
// preprocessor, and renaming one is trivial. The requirement is that it is never
// silent — the pre-ADR behaviour skipped the second header and produced a wrong
// runtime value with a single warning.
#include "mod-a.cnx"
#include "mod_a.cnx"

u32 main() {
    u8 first <- Alpha.one();
    u8 second <- Beta.two();

    if (first != 1) return 1;
    if (second != 2) return 2;

    return 0;
}
